<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohegan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mohegan are an Algonquian-speaking Native American people of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>. In the 1630s their sachem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uncas">Uncas</a> broke away from the Pequot and allied with the English colonists, fighting beside them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pequot-war">Pequot War</a> of 1637. They became the leading Native allies of Connecticut, and the Mohegan Tribe, federally recognised in 1994, has its reservation near Uncasville.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohegan.jpg" alt="Mohegan" width="320" height="505" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Image courtesy of the Mohegan Tribe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emma_Fielding_Baker_2.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
